Package: promoterPrimerMapper
Type: Package
Title: Bisulfite-Sequencing PCR Primer Design for Gene Promoters
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("Ilya", "Kisselev", email = "kisselev.iy@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Author: Ilya Kisselev [aut]
Maintainer: Ilya Kisselev <kisselev.iy@gmail.com>
Description: Selects transcription start sites from transcript annotation,
    extracts transcription-oriented promoter sequence, and designs
    bisulfite-sequencing PCR (BSP) primers: candidates are enumerated on the
    bisulfite-converted template under bisulfite-specific rules, scored with
    Primer3, paired around a TSS-relative target, and checked for off-target
    products against a Bismark-prepared converted genome with Bowtie2. Primers
    from external tools such as MethPrimer can be mapped back to genomic
    coordinates. Includes a local Shiny interface.
License: GPL-3 + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
SystemRequirements: Primer3 (>= 2.5.0) for primer design; Bowtie2 and
    Bismark (optional) for the specificity check.
Imports:
